{
  "$comment": [
    "Cross-platform Bubble parity fixtures. ONE file, read by two engines:",
    "  dev/bubble-engine-parity.test.js                    runs these through app/js/bubble-engine.js",
    "  ios/WatchBubbleEngine/Tests/.../BubbleEngineParityTests.swift   reads THIS path, never a copy",
    "A copied fixture is a second source of truth and defeats the point.",
    "",
    "Expectations are recorded from the JavaScript engine, which is authoritative:",
    "  node dev/bubble-engine-parity.test.js --update",
    "That is a deliberate act, like re-running the client generator. Review the diff,",
    "and bump bubbleEngineVersion when the answers change on purpose.",
    "",
    "Every case names why it exists. The corners are the point — a fixture set that",
    "only covers a mid-iron from the middle of the fairway would pass on an engine",
    "that had lost handedness, lost the ghost bag, or fabricated an aim offset."
  ],
  "bubbleEngineVersion": "bubble-engine-v3",
  "tolerances": {
    "$comment": "Per-field, because 0.1 means different things to a metre, a degree and a latitude. 1e-7 degrees is ~11mm.",
    "metres": 0.1,
    "degrees": 0.01,
    "distanceM": 0.5,
    "coordinate": 1e-7
  },
  "bags": {
    "$comment": "A real account bag, longest first the way gdNormaliseShotBagRows sorts it. totalM omitted so the roll-out preset derives it — the wrist receives finished numbers, but the fixture pins the derivation too.",
